     "result_text_tail": " lose about $18M a year.\n5. **The software is the better bet.** About 10 new contracts cover the $0.8M a year of hires, and 9 grocers are already at the late stage. The deck ends with three conditions for reopening the operator question.\n\n**Choices I made in your place**\n- **Audience:** the board, deciding whether to approve or reject. **Theme:** navy.\n- **Two meanings of \"contribution per order\":** before and after dark-store costs. Each slide says which one it uses.\n- **The $9.5M cash need:** the pack doesn't say whether it includes the software business's own $0.4M monthly burn. The cash chart uses the reading most favourable to the plan, and a note on the slide says that under the other reading cash runs out before month 18.\n- **Network sizing ($18M loss):** this is my estimate. It assumes all stores run at full volume with no ramp-up, and those assumptions are shown on the slide.\n- **Owners on the next steps:** these are generic roles (Board, CEO, Founders, Finance lead, Operations lead), because the pack doesn't give the team structure.\n\nI couldn't look at the slides as images because there's no viewer in this environment. I checked layout with the renderer's overflow warnings, and none are left, then read every slide's text back from the file. It's worth a quick look in PowerPoint. Small cards round to one decimal, so the formula strip on page 8 shows \u2212$6.2 next to \u2212$6.17 on the chart.\n\nIf you want, I can try another theme or turn any estimate into a sensitivity range."
